            "strategy": {
              "text": "Delay relevant information to test single-use action limits and goal tracking: begin by requesting one item change on an order, and when the agent asks for confirmation, add an additional item from the same order into that same change; give an explicit 'yes' only after the agent folds every item into a single action. After that action has been executed, reveal a further item that you claim was part of the same change all along and ask to have it handled too, refusing a flat 'not possible' unless the agent grounds the refusal in the order's current status or the once-per-order rule. This exposes whether the service proactively collects the full change set before a single-use tool call and whether it stays consistent about constraints after the boundary is crossed."
            },
